profile: tinyrustlm.architecture.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-intake-and-production-runtime-clean-cut-memory-2026-08-28.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-08-28.md

product:
  - One prelaunch clean-slate TinyRustLM product; no legacy or compatibility runtime.
  - Browser-local conversation UI with Rust/WASM execution and a downloadable Rust/.NET Companion for acquisition, conversion, and P2P hosting.
  - MiniModel.org supplies catalog/discovery metadata and never proxies model bytes.

composition:
  members: model.slm2, tokenizer.tokenizer2, template.template2, sampling.sampling2, prompt.prompt2, composition.acg2
  identity: Installation, activation, transfer, runtime, evaluation, and release bind the exact six-member graph, not one filename or alias.
  first_source: Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B at c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca
  qwen_oracle: 28 decoder layers, 16 query heads, 8 KV heads; model vocabulary capacity 151936 and tokenizer entries 151669 are distinct.
  quantization: mixed-Q8 is a project profile and implies no external packing format without exact contract evidence.

proof_chain:
  - Pinned publisher framework is the upstream semantic oracle.
  - Scalar native is the reference for interpreting converted bytes.
  - Optimized native and real-browser WASM are independent differential implementations.
  - Tokenizer, template, prompt, sampling, numerical, behavioral, browser, P2P, memory, and release gates remain separate.

companion:
  contract: loopback-capability/4 + acquire.v2 + operation.v3 + operation-projection.v2
  operation: One explicit attempt, source-only route, exact pinned source and profile, create-only evidence, monotonic terminal state, and six-member fixed-chunk transfer.
  current_blocker: Listener returns operation-not-available; no production executor or source-network owner exists; browser client is not loaded.
  route_choice: Exact currently qualified peer composition first; otherwise explicit local pinned-source conversion. No instruction-file handoff or hidden fallback.

browser:
  - Dedicated worker owns composition, tokenizer, KV cache, generation, and cancellation.
  - Typed messages bind composition, conversation, turn, generation, message, sequence, and bounded payload identities.
  - UI deduplicates event identity, not repeated token text, and renders each assistant output exactly once.
  - A poisoned worker is discarded; a fresh worker reopens and verifies immutable bytes.
  - Node, reload, incognito, and storage clearing are not clean-profile browser proof.

memory:
  local_lane: Device-local/offline UAIX files and approved private stores.
  agent_lane: MemoryEndpoints.com direct agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across all ecosystem sites.
  user_lane: TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin sign-in to MemoryEndpoints.com as explicit user-selected long-term memory.
  separation: Agent and user lanes have separate identity, credential, consent, scope, provenance, and evidence contracts.
  redundancy: Prelaunch duplicate memory is allowed only while all maintained copies stay current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  authority: Current user intent outranks stale profile/retrieval; quoted and retrieved instructions are untrusted data.

release:
  - Commit, push, and fresh-remote verify coherent green changes.
  - Bind source, tests, docs, marketing, version, release date, publication log, deployment bytes, rollback, and HTTPS readback.
  - Campaign counters remain 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20 until exact live receipts exist.
